"_gate_spread":-0.08802003067875633,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.8309160068286854,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.13045087372856412,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.024365957007597527,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":25.6,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.057316732207943574,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":74.8,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.13564677689572538,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01021,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"PubMatic, Inc., a technology company, engages in the provision of a cloud infrastructure platform that enables real time programmatic advertising transactions for digital content creators, advertisers, agencies, agency trading desks, and demand side platforms worldwide. Its PubMatic SSP is a sell side platform for the purchase and sale of digital advertising inventory for publishers and buyers. The company also provides OpenWrap, a header bidding solution; Connect, a solution that provides additional data and insights to publishers and buyers; Activate, which allows buyers to execute direct deals on its platform across publisher inventory; Convert, a commerce media solution; and Identity Hub, an ID management tool for publishers that leverages specialized technology infrastructure to simplify alternative identifier marketplace. Its platform supports an array of ad formats and digital device types, including mobile app, mobile web, desktop, display, video, over the top video, connected television, and media. The company was incorporated in 2006 and is based in Redwood City, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Rajeev K. Goel | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $275K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $65K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $37K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["PubMatic, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $811M market cap on $283M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -8.0pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 65% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $67M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -14.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 5.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -8.0pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 57% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5702652078157411},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PubMatic Q3 2026 Earnings Preview (NASDAQ:PUBM)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668230-pubmatic-q3-2026-earnings-preview","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794004563.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Earnings To Watch: PubMatic Inc (PUBM) Q3 2026 -- GF Value Sees 9% Upside","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/earnings-watch-pubmatic-inc-pubm-122515545.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793967915.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"PubMatic, Inc. (NASDAQ:PUBM) Stock Has Consensus Price Target of $19.73","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/pubmatic-inc-nasdaqpubm-stock-has-consensus-price-target-of-19-73.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793962743.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"(PUBM) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/PUBM_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_103026112202_1793373722.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793373722.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Fox Roku Deal Puts PubMatic Stock In Focus For Connected TV Investors","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nasdaq-pubm/pubmatic/news/fox-roku-deal-puts-pubmatic-stock-in-focus-for-connected-tv","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793989629.852,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Strategus Partners with PubMatic to Unlock Smarter CTV Performance for Advertisers in Live Sport